        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0-4> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Gasterosteus doryssus_early specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-gasterosteus-doryssus-early-turing-wavelength-s0.py> ;
    schema:about "Gasterosteus doryssus_early" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: An emergent PDE spiral, a second assessor, a machine-checked Lean build, or a signed nanopublication.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Early-chronospecies Schnakenberg field at λ near 32.86 µm, equal-diffusion ablation, D_u sweep, diffusion-ratio sweep, four-seed ensemble, and a successor integration at D_u × (41.50/32.86)^2.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: m=2 ocellus GIF whose amplitude follows RMS(u), CV 85.9 against the gallery photograph.",
        "reported_in_source: Hunt, Bell & Travis (2008) and Bell, Travis & Blouw (2006): pelvic reduction along the Truckee G. doryssus series, complete pelvis at the start.",
        "reported_in_source: Stuart, Travis & Bell (2020): Pitx1 in that fossil lineage. Nakamasu et al. (2009) and Kondo & Miura (2010): teleost chromatophore Turing patterns.",
        "reported_in_source: Turing (1952) dispersion relation and Schnakenberg (1979) kinetics.",
        "transfer_boundary: 32.86 µm is the assigned cellular-detail rung, not a spacing published by Bell, Hunt, or Stuart.",
        "transfer_boundary: The gallery spiral is not a Truckee thin section. Its 81.08 µm band is not λ_c.",
        "transfer_boundary: The successor diffusivity scaling is a model of wavelength lengthening tied to pelvic reduction, not a measurement at 10.01 Ma." ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Gasterosteus doryssus_early (Late Miocene (Truckee Fm, 10.02 Ma))" ;
